  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h2>»idChip« or »idLabel«?</h2>",
   "body": "<p>Both carry a DataMatrix code and make tools uniquely identifiable. Which solution fits depends on the application.</p>",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "/fileadmin/02_Products/idChip/zoller_idchip_vergleich_idchip.webp",
     "w": 1390,
     "h": 869,
     "alt": "»idChip«",
     "title": "»idChip«",
     "caption": "<figcaption> <h3>»idChip«</h3> <p>The better choice for rotating tools: firmly integrated in the holder, protected there and still clearly visible.</p> </figcaption>"
    },
    {
     "src": "/fileadmin/02_Products/idChip/zoller_idchip_vergleich_idlabel.webp",
     "w": 1385,
     "h": 866,
     "alt": "»idLabel«",
     "title": "»idLabel«",
     "caption": "<figcaption> <h3>»idLabel«</h3> <p>Recommended for turning tools and fixtures that are not used in rotation: the resin-coated label is attached firmly and securely to the tool holder.</p> </figcaption>"
    }
   ],
